From: Tiaoge-tou <85100527+Tiaoge-tou@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:29:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Pad watcher: the host reads Silksong's game state and
 publishes the pad mode, tab and page

The host half of the touch pad's scene awareness (patch port 0069, group D part 1 of the port inventory), carried from the Tiaoge-tou/nxnative fork.

hle_hid.c gains the watcher: with the pad skin on (DM_PAD_SKIN) and a known class layout for the build (k_pad_layouts, Silksong's GameManager / UIManager / hero statics), a host thread reads the game's own state objects and publishes the pad mode (play, loading, cutscene skippable or not, inventory, title, controller page), the inventory tab and the UI page. Any doubt reads as play, so the pad never hides on a guess. dm_input.h declares dm_pad_mode / dm_pad_tab / dm_pad_page for the iOS gamepad, the only caller. dm/tools/docs_patches.py classifies the k_pad_layouts host binding the watcher relies on.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Silksong pad watcher: pad mode, inventory tab and UI page from the game's own state (PROJECT.md Phase 2)
Issue: Tiaoge-tou/NX2Apple PROJECT.md Phase 2

---
 dm/host/dm_input.h       |  22 ++++++++
 dm/host/hle_hid.c        | 117 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dm/tools/docs_patches.py |   2 +
 3 files changed, 141 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dm/host/dm_input.h b/dm/host/dm_input.h
index f784e7c..e0abef1 100644
--- a/dm/host/dm_input.h
+++ b/dm/host/dm_input.h
@@ -13,6 +13,28 @@ enum {
 #define DM_STICK_MAX 32767
 void dm_input_set(uint64_t buttons, int32_t lx, int32_t ly, int32_t rx, int32_t ry);
 uint64_t dm_input_samples(void);   // Cumulative number of times the game has sampled the controller
+// Pad mode for the touch gamepad's skin (hle_hid.c): 0 = play (the pad shows), 1 = a loading state (the pad hides), 2 = a cutscene that
+// cannot be skipped (the pad hides, its recall switch shows), 3 = a cutscene that can be skipped (the pad hides, the recall switch and a
+// skip key show), 4 = the inventory (the bag layout replaces the pad), 5 = the title screen (the stick and two letter keys show),
+// 6 = a controller page (every key shows, as a letter). Read from the game's own state objects by a host thread, only with the pad
+// skin on (DM_PAD_SKIN) and only for a build with a known class layout. -1 while the watcher has not published yet (it derives its
+// first mode from the first state inside its range), so the pad stays hidden while the game loads; a build with no layout publishes 0
+// at once, and any doubt once the watcher is running -- a class not ready, a null link, a state value out of range -- reads as 0, so
+// the pad never hides on a guess. The iOS gamepad polls it; other front ends never call it and see no change
+int dm_pad_mode(void);
+// The inventory's current tab for the same pad (hle_hid.c, the same watcher): 0 = items, 1 = crests, 2 = quests, 3 = journal,
+// 4 = map, read from the hero's own field; -1 while the hero does not resolve or the value sits outside the tab range (the tab
+// keeps its last value while the inventory is closed). The bag layout's X key shows only on the crests tab; an unknown tab shows it
+int dm_pad_tab(void);
+// The UI manager's current page for the same pad (hle_hid.c, the same watcher): 1 = the title screen, 2 = options, 3 = the
+// controller page, 6 = the save select, 7 = sound, 12 = game options, 13 = achievements, 19 = extras, 20 = the key-binding
+// page, read from the UI manager's own field (the game and UI state enums sit at 1/1 across all of them); -1 until the
+// watcher first reads the UI manager (no mode is published before that, so the pad stays hidden), and -1 while it does
+// not resolve or the value sits outside the page range. At game state 1 the watcher turns pages 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 12 and 19
+// into pad mode 5, page 13 into pad mode 7 and page 20 into pad mode 6; at game state 5 (the pause: 17 = its menu, 10 =
+// its save-and-quit confirm, and an options branch that reuses the title branch's page values) page 20 alone turns into
+// pad mode 6 and every other page into pad mode 5; every other page at game state 1 leaves the mode to the states
+int dm_pad_page(void);
 // The cheat VM's key mask (hle_cheats.c): every input source's button bits (0..15 in the enum above) ORed and the
 // merged axes' eight stick-direction bits (16..23), one flat bitset; no latches are consumed (the game's own reads
 // keep them). The NpadButton SL / SR bits (24 / 25) never fire: no input source of this host reports them
diff --git a/dm/host/hle_hid.c b/dm/host/hle_hid.c
index 90e798e..49fc2b4 100644
--- a/dm/host/hle_hid.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_hid.c
@@ -63,6 +63,123 @@ static void script_set(uint64_t buttons, int32_t lx, int32_t ly, int32_t rx, int
     shake_note();
 }
 uint64_t dm_input_samples(void) { return (uint64_t)atomic_load(&g_sampling); }
+// ---- Pad mode from the game's own state (the touch gamepad hides in cutscenes and loads and switches to its bag layout in the inventory; DmGamepad.m polls dm_pad_mode) ----
+// The class objects of an IL2CPP game sit in slots in main's image, one per class the runtime has loaded: slot -> class object ->
+// (once its ready flag at +0xe4 is set) its static fields at +0xb8 -> the singleton instance at a per-class offset in the statics.
+// The layout below is per build, like every fixed guest offset in this host, and follows the offsets the touch port of this same
+// build uses (MZhao-ouo/Touchable, MIT): GameManager's instance at statics +0x8, its game state at +0x20 (7 = a cutscene; 2, 3 and
+// 6 = loading states), its input handler at +0xa8, whose skip mode at +0x84 is 0 or 1 while the cutscene can be skipped;
+// UIManager's instance at statics +0x10, its UI state at +0x64 (3 = a cutscene, 2 = loading); the hero's instance at its own
+// class's statics +0x8, with the byte at +0x8ac set while the inventory is open (the two state enums do not change for it), which
+// with game state 4 (playing) is mode 4, the bag. The hero also carries the inventory's current tab as a u32 at +0x278 (0 items,
+// 1 crests, 2 quests, 3 journal, 4 map; its neighbours sit still while only it steps with the tab, found by a wide dump across
+// all five tabs; it keeps its last value while the inventory is closed), published through dm_pad_tab for the bag layout's X
+// key, which shows on the crests tab only. The UI manager also carries its current page as a u32 at +0x68 (1 = the title
+// screen, 2 = options, 3 = the controller page, 6 = the save select, 7 = sound, 12 = game options, 13 = achievements,
+// 19 = extras, 20 = the key-binding page; the two state enums sit at 1/1 across all of them, so only this field tells them
+// apart, found by a wide dump across the pages in the memory-diff probe's format, every one of its twelve dumps fitting,
+// the later pages read off the watcher's own page log), published through dm_pad_page: at game state 1, pages 1, 2, 3, 6,
+// 7, 12 and 19 are mode 5 (the menu pages: the stick and its two letter keys only; the controller page among them, which
+// needs only A to enter the key-binding page and B to go back), page 13 alone is mode 7 (achievements: the stick and B
+// alone -- the list scrolls on the stick and B is the page's only way out) and page 20 alone is mode 6 (the key-binding
+// page). At game state 5 (the pause) the same field runs the pause's own pages -- 17 the pause menu, 10 the save-and-quit
+// confirm -- and the pause's options branch reuses the title branch's page values (2, 3, 7, 12, 20, read off the
+// watcher's page log across a paused walk of the whole branch): there page 20 alone is mode 6 and every other page is
+// mode 5, the pause's transitions among them included. An instance counts only while the
+// native object behind it lives (the pointer at +0x10). The mode starts unpublished (dm_pad_mode reads -1) until the watcher
+// first derives it from a state inside its range, so the pad stays hidden while the game loads to its title screen; a build
+// with no layout publishes 0 at once, and once the watcher is running, fail-safe throughout: a class not ready, a null link,
+// or a state value outside its range reads as mode 0 (play), so a layout that does not fit the build can never hide the pad
+typedef struct { const char *build; uint64_t game_class, ui_class, player_class; } pad_layout_t;
+static const pad_layout_t k_pad_layouts[] = {
+    { "fc9ea4ccc955d5799f37752b2d730b31", 0x7e14880, 0x7e195b8, 0x7e176b0 },   // Hollow Knight: Silksong, the build in its game.tsv
+};
+static _Atomic int g_pad_mode;
+static _Atomic int g_pad_tab;   // the inventory's current tab (dm_pad_tab): -1 until the watcher first reads the hero
+static _Atomic int g_pad_page;   // the UI manager's current page (dm_pad_page): -1 until the watcher first reads the UI manager
+static const void *pad_static(const uint8_t *base, uint64_t slot, uint64_t inst_off) {
+    const void *klass = *(const void *const *)(base + slot);
+    if (!klass || ((uintptr_t)klass & 7)) return NULL;
+    if (!*(const int32_t *)((const uint8_t *)klass + 0xe4)) return NULL;   // the class is not initialised yet
+    const void *statics = *(const void *const *)((const uint8_t *)klass + 0xb8);
+    if (!statics) return NULL;
+    const void *inst = *(const void *const *)((const uint8_t *)statics + inst_off);
+    if (!inst || !*(const void *const *)((const uint8_t *)inst + 0x10)) return NULL;   // no live object behind it
+    return inst;
+}
+static void *pad_mode_main(void *arg) {
+    (void)arg;
+    const pad_layout_t *lay = NULL; const uint8_t *base = NULL;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 240 && !lay; i++) {   // main and its class pointers land as the guest starts: wait for the build's layout, up to about a minute
+        const char *b = dm_main_build();
+        for (unsigned k = 0; k < sizeof k_pad_layouts / sizeof *k_pad_layouts && !lay; k++) if (!strcmp(k_pad_layouts[k].build, b)) lay = &k_pad_layouts[k];
+        if (lay) for (int m = 0; m < g_nmod; m++) if (!strcmp(g_mod[m].name, "main")) base = g_mod[m].base;
+        if (!lay || !base) { struct timespec ts = { 0, 250000000 }; nanosleep(&ts, NULL); }
+    }
+    if (!lay || !base) { atomic_store(&g_pad_mode, 0); LOG("[pad] no game-state layout for this build; the pad stays as it is"); return NULL; }
+    LOG("[pad] watching the game state for cutscenes and loads (build %s)", lay->build);
+    const char *be = getenv("DM_PAD_BAG");   // the bag mode's own switch, read once: off (0), mode 4 never happens and the pad behaves as if the feature were not there
+    int bag_on = !be || atoi(be);
+    if (!bag_on) LOG("[pad] bag mode off (DM_PAD_BAG=0)");
+    int cur = -1;
+    for (;;) {
+        int mode = 0, known = 0;
+        const void *gm = pad_static(base, lay->game_class, 0x8);
+        const void *um = pad_static(base, lay->ui_class, 0x10);
+        int gs = gm ? *(const int32_t *)((const uint8_t *)gm + 0x20) : -1;
+        int us = um ? *(const int32_t *)((const uint8_t *)um + 0x64) : -1;
+        static int pgs = -2, pus = -2;   // state probe: log the raw game/UI states whenever either changes (read-only)
+        if (gs != pgs || us != pus) { pgs = gs; pus = us; LOG("[pad] state gs=%d us=%d", gs, us); }
+        const void *pl = pad_static(base, lay->player_class, 0x8);   // the hero: the byte at +0x8ac is set while the inventory is open
+        int inv = pl ? *(const uint8_t *)((const uint8_t *)pl + 0x8ac) : -1;   // -1 when the hero does not resolve: no bag, never a bag by accident
+        int tab = pl ? *(const int32_t *)((const uint8_t *)pl + 0x278) : -1;   // the inventory's current tab, on the same hero (keeps its last value while the inventory is closed)
+        if (tab < 0 || tab > 4) tab = -1;   // a value outside the tab range means the layout does not fit: unknown, and the front end shows the bag's X key rather than hiding it on a guess
+        static int ptab = -2;
+        if (tab != ptab) { ptab = tab; atomic_store(&g_pad_tab, tab); LOG("[pad] tab %d", tab); }
+        int page = um ? *(const int32_t *)((const uint8_t *)um + 0x68) : -1;   // the UI manager's current page, next to its UI state
+        if (page < 0 || page > 64) page = -1;   // a value outside the page range means the layout does not fit: unknown, and no page mode follows from it
+        static int ppage = -2;
+        if (page != ppage) { ppage = page; atomic_store(&g_pad_page, page); LOG("[pad] page %d", page); }
+        if (gs >= 0 && gs <= 7 && us >= 0 && us <= 6) {   // a state outside its range means the layout does not fit: never hide
+            known = 1;
+            if (gs == 7 || us == 3) {
+                mode = 2;
+                const void *ih = gm ? *(const void *const *)((const uint8_t *)gm + 0xa8) : NULL;
+                if (ih && *(const void *const *)((const uint8_t *)ih + 0x10)) { int sm = *(const int32_t *)((const uint8_t *)ih + 0x84); if (sm == 0 || sm == 1) mode = 3; }
+            } else if (gs == 2 || gs == 3 || gs == 6 || us == 2) mode = 1;
+            else if (gs == 5 && page == 20) mode = 6;   // the pause's key-binding page, on the title branch's terms: every key, as a letter, so it can be worked
+            else if (gs == 5) mode = 5;   // the pause (its menu, its save-and-quit confirm and its options branch's other pages, transitions among them included): the stick and its two letter keys only
+            else if (gs == 1 && (page == 1 || page == 2 || page == 3 || page == 6 || page == 7 || page == 12 || page == 19)) mode = 5;   // the menu pages (the title screen, the options branch's pages, the save select, the controller page and the extras page with them): the stick and its two letter keys only
+            else if (gs == 1 && page == 13) mode = 7;   // the achievements page: the stick and B alone (the list scrolls on the stick)
+            else if (gs == 1 && page == 20) mode = 6;   // the key-binding page: every key, as a letter, so it can be worked
+            else if (bag_on && gs == 4 && inv == 1) mode = 4;   // the inventory: both enums stay at play while it is open, only the hero's byte tells
+        }
+        if ((known || cur >= 0) && mode != cur) { cur = mode; atomic_store(&g_pad_mode, mode); LOG("[pad] mode %d (%s)", mode, mode == 7 ? "achievements" : mode == 6 ? (gs == 5 ? "settings, paused" : "settings") : mode == 5 ? (gs == 5 ? "pause" : "title") : mode == 4 ? "bag" : mode == 3 ? "cutscene, skippable" : mode == 2 ? "cutscene" : mode == 1 ? "loading" : "play"); }   // until the first state inside its range derives a mode, nothing is published: the mode stays -1 and the pad stays hidden
+        struct timespec ts = { 0, 100000000 }; nanosleep(&ts, NULL);
+    }
+    return NULL;
+}
+static void pad_mode_start(void) {
+    atomic_store(&g_pad_tab, -1);   // unknown until the watcher reads the hero (it may never start: then the tab stays unknown)
+    atomic_store(&g_pad_page, -1);   // unknown until the watcher reads the UI manager, on the same terms
+    const char *e = getenv("DM_PAD_SKIN");   // the reader exists for the pad skin only: without it no thread starts and the mode stays 0
+    if (!e || !atoi(e)) return;
+    atomic_store(&g_pad_mode, -1);   // unpublished until the watcher derives its first mode: with the skin on, the pad stays hidden while the game loads
+    pthread_t th; if (!pthread_create(&th, NULL, pad_mode_main, NULL)) pthread_detach(th);
+}
+static pthread_once_t pad_mode_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+int dm_pad_mode(void) {
+    pthread_once(&pad_mode_once, pad_mode_start);
+    return atomic_load(&g_pad_mode);
+}
+int dm_pad_tab(void) {
+    pthread_once(&pad_mode_once, pad_mode_start);
+    return atomic_load(&g_pad_tab);
+}
+int dm_pad_page(void) {
+    pthread_once(&pad_mode_once, pad_mode_start);
+    return atomic_load(&g_pad_page);
+}
 // DM_KEYS scripted input (for tests): "seconds:key[+key][~hold seconds][*count/interval seconds],...", e.g. "8:A,12:A,15:Down~0.5,16:A+B,40:A*80/2" (A every 2 s from 40 s on, 80 times). Key names A B X Y LS RS L R ZL ZR (plus the sticks LLeft LUp LRight LDown and RLeft RUp RRight RDown) Plus Minus Left Up Right Down, left stick LLeft LUp LRight LDown,
 //   L<x>/<y> and R<x>/<y> = a stick tilted part way (each -1 to 1, y up: a cursor that a full tilt sweeps past its target), T<x>x<y> = a touch at normalized picture coordinates (origin top left) for the hold time, and Shake = the controller shaken for the hold time (at least one whole shake);
 //   held 0.15 s by default, at most KEY_STEPS steps (counted after repeats are expanded). Goes through player 1's scripted path (script_set), ORed with keyboard / touch and player 1's controller, none overrides another. Times are counted from host start.
diff --git a/dm/tools/docs_patches.py b/dm/tools/docs_patches.py
